Phase2 matrix experiments from plan:
1. Hard negative mining (reviews/cohorts/predictions) → reduce FP. Dependency: manual/rule mining + labels; cost M; metric: test precision at recall≥0.95, bootstrap CI lower bound > baseline. Guardrail: no label definition change; add negatives only in train or new split.
2. Section-aware chunking → reduce FN. Dependency: PDF/XML structure; cost L (re-encode; but Phase2 can use cache? Section-aware requires re-encoding, GPU); metric: recall/F2; guardrail: keep frozen encoder, no fine-tune.
3. Supplement PubMed abstracts → improve no-abstract subset (210/974). Dependency: network or existing library (Phase 1 forbids PubMed crawl, Phase 2 optional); metric: recall on empty_abstract stratum; guardrail: legal/API rate; no label change.
4. Switch primary model to B → simplify features (C ≈ B). Dependency: existing ablation; cost S; metric: AP/ROC non-inferiority, dim -2; guardrail: keep C if no gain.
5. CUDA re-encoding → speed iteration. Dependency GPU; cost M; metric: encoding time, not model quality; guardrail: verify cache parity.
6. Light adapter fine-tune → last resort. Dependency label quality + CV still below target; cost XL; metric: GroupCV AP/precision; guardrail: freeze eval splits, no leakage; only if 1-3 fail.

Add columns: priority, expected effect, cost, dependency, primary acceptance metric, risk/guardrail.

